Expansion sound cards: Toccata, Prelude, Prelude 1200 and UAESND

sndboard.c was compiled with WITH_TOCCATA undefined, so every board in it was a stub. It holds
MacroSystem's Toccata and ACT's Prelude (Zorro II, AD1848/CS4231A codecs with a FIFO), the
Prelude 1200 on the A1200 clock port, and WinUAE's own UAESND Zorro II/III board - the one
WinUAE's AHI driver uses. Each mixes into the Paula output through audio_enable_stream(), so
nothing changes on the libretro side.

- sysconfig.h: WITH_TOCCATA on (all platforms; nothing here is host-specific).
- sndboard.c, for a C build: WinUAE compiles it as C++ with MSVC, which accepts an extern
  forward declaration followed by a static definition, and NULL for a uaecptr. The FM801 and
  SOLO1 PCI cards go under WITH_PCI (pci.c is empty without it). The vsync, volume and init
  hooks lived inside the HAVE_X86 block with QEMU's audio glue and the WASAPI recording code;
  without HAVE_X86 they are provided for the boards above, and recording input reads nothing.
- libretro-core.c: puae_sound_board (disabled, toccata, prelude, prelude1200, uaesnd_z2,
  uaesnd_z3) writes <board>_rom_file=:ENABLED, the row WinUAE writes for an expansion board.

The AHI define stays off: it is WinUAE's older DirectSound-backed AHI emulation
(ahidsound.cpp), which this tree does not have; UAESND replaced it.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

